      "body": "Native plugin distribution can replace copied plugin content, while Rig still needs bounded ownership and wiring checks. Both Claude Code 2.1.270 and Codex 0.154.0 install the shared synthetic source in both Rig orders, execute the updated 1.0.1 package, and uninstall without losing the tested Rig edits.\n\nRuler 0.3.44 deletes foreign Rig skills/agents when projecting overlapping directories. Codex import safely migrates configuration but replay does not propagate changed source. The A/F gate is GO for remaining investigation, limited to installer/compatibility/lifecycle scope.\n\nEvidence: 65 passed candidate properties, 15 failed, 8 unverified. Independent review approved conditional ADAPT; validator checks 447 complete command records and 176 snapshots. Actual hook enforcement, model routing and complete native-cache customization/Rig removal semantics remain unverified. All experiments use synthetic fixtures and isolated homes.\n\nValidation: Ubuntu native lifecycle run 34830163055 succeeded; lightweight evidence checks and final branch CI must be green before merge. Report, provenance, ownership tables, numeric rubric, review and reproduction commands are included.\n",
