      "body": "Spec Kit 1.0.6 already provides manifest-aware integration upgrades and removal, so this spike measures the lifecycle value still added by Rig 0.9.0. It exercises both install orders, exact-path collisions, deliberate deletion, user edits, cross-release upgrade, offline replay, and a bounded conservative Rig-removal prototype.\n\nVerdict: ADAPT. Observed gaps include restored deleted skills, metadata byte drift, loss of Codex registration after repeat force-init, and Windows LF/CRLF settings drift. Native integration upgrade preserves Codex registration; a bounded newline-only repair restores Windows ownership. The removal prototype preserves Spec Kit and executes its feature script afterwards.\n\nValidation: final Linux and Windows hosted runs succeeded; independent review corrections are resolved. The requirement ledger has 42 passed, 7 failed candidate properties and 5 unverified scenarios. The artifact checker validates 292 complete commands and 97 successful git snapshots. Published Rig integrity, full baseline diff and manifest are retained; fixtures and installed payload remain untracked. No production repository was modified.\n",
